# Shell scripts MUST keep LF endings.
# A .sh file checked out with CRLF fails in bash with an opaque
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M" error - the shebang line ends in \r.
# This repo is developed on Windows, so without this rule git would convert
# them on checkout and every bash tool here would break.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Python is LF-safe and cross-platform; keep it consistent for clean diffs.
*.py text eol=lf

# Docs and data: normalise on commit, leave the working copy to the platform.
*.md text
*.txt text
*.json text
*.yml text
*.yaml text

# Never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
